twisted.mail.smtp.SMTP.receivedHeader no longer raises TypeError when the default (no custom IMessageDelivery) header generation is used, and now neutralizes CR and LF bytes in the client-supplied HELO/EHLO name so they cannot inject additional headers into the server-generated Received trace field. The transport-level peer address continues to be recorded separately from the untrusted client-asserted name, and Received headers supplied inside DATA are still delivered verbatim as untrusted message content.
